          <strong>What is a Specialized Investment Fund (SIF)?</strong><br />
          A <strong>Specialized Investment Fund (SIF)</strong> is a SEBI-regulated investment vehicle introduced under the "New Asset Class" framework. Positioned strategically between traditional Mutual Funds and high-ticket Portfolio Management Services (PMS) / Alternative Investment Funds (AIFs), SIF features a <strong>minimum investment threshold of ₹10 Lakhs</strong> per investor. It allows Asset Management Companies (AMCs) to deploy sophisticated investment strategies—such as Long-Short equity, inverse downside hedging, factor quant models, and structured debt—within the investor-friendly regulatory framework of a mutual fund trust.
        </p>
