      <h2>The Major Tax Advantage: Why SIF Beats PMS for Active Investors</h2>
      <p>
        One of the biggest hidden costs of Portfolio Management Services (PMS) is <strong>tax friction</strong>:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>In a PMS:</strong> Your manager buys and sells stocks inside your own Demat account. Every single rebalancing move, profit booking, or defensive trim generates an actionable taxable event on your PAN. If your PMS manager trades frequently, you can accumulate dozens of pages of short-term capital gains (taxed at 20%) and long-term capital gains (taxed at 12.5%), creating severe tax drag and accounting headaches.</li>
        <li><strong>In a SIF:</strong> Because SIF is structured as a mutual fund trust, all internal portfolio trading, derivatives positioning, and tactical shifts are <strong>100% tax-exempt at the fund level</strong>. You do not pay a single rupee in capital gains tax until you choose to redeem your units. This lets your capital compound uninterrupted.</li>
      </ul>

