            <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--text-head);">How is SIF different from AIF Category III?</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--text-body); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6;">
              AIF Category III requires a minimum ₹1 Crore investment, allows higher leverage, and is typically structured as a private placement trust with monthly or quarterly valuation updates. SIF requires only ₹10 Lakhs, features automated daily NAVs, and is accessible under standard AMC onboarding. Read our comprehensive <a href="/blog/how-to-track-aif-sif-portfolio-india/" style="color: var(--primary-glow);">AIF vs SIF tracking guide</a> to learn more.
